<title>USA: The top 10 movies at the U.S. box office.</title>
<headline>The top 10 movies at the U.S. box office.</headline>
<dateline>LOS ANGELES</dateline>
<text>
<p>Following are the top 10 movies at the box office over the Friday-to-Sunday weekend, according to studio estimates collected by Exhibitor Relations Co. Inc. Final data are due Monday. (Rank last week in parentheses).</p>
<p>    1 (*) Star Wars ....................... $36.2 million</p>
<p>    2 (1) Jerry Maguire .................... $5.6 million</p>
<p>    3 (6) Scream ........................... $4.8 million</p>
<p>    4 (4) Metro ............................ $4.4 million</p>
<p>    5=(5) Evita ............................ $4.3 million</p>
<p>    5=(3) Beverly Hills Ninja .............. $4.3 million</p>
<p>    7 (2) In Love And War .................. $3.9 million</p>
<p>    8 (7) The Relic ........................ $2.9 million</p>
<p>    9 (*) Gridlock'd ....................... $2.8 million</p>
<p>   10(11) Mother ........................... $2.6 million</p>
<p>   10 (9) Michael .......................... $2.6 million</p>
<p>NOTE: &quot;Star Wars&quot; is released by 20th Century Fox, a unit of News Corp..</p>
<p>&quot;Jerry Maguire&quot; and &quot;Beverly Hills Ninja&quot; are released by TriStar Pictures, a unit of Sony Corp..</p>
<p>&quot;Scream&quot; is released by Miramax Films, a unit of Walt Disney Co.. &quot;Metro&quot; and &quot;Evita&quot; are released by Disney.</p>
<p>&quot;In Love and War&quot; and &quot;Michael&quot; are released by New Line Cinema, both units of Time Warner Inc..</p>
<p>&quot;The Relic&quot; and &quot;Mother&quot; are released by Paramount Pictures, a unit of Viacom Inc..</p>
<p>&quot;Gridlock'd&quot; is released by Gramercy Pictures, a unit of PolyGram NV..</p>
